<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
	Planner's only entitlements file. There is no local-only variant: every
	build signs with a real development certificate and carries the iCloud keys.

	That means a checkout does not build without signing set up. Concretely, a
	developer needs an Apple Developer Program membership, an Apple Development
	certificate in the login keychain, and DEVELOPMENT_TEAM set on the target.
	Codesign refuses the iCloud keys below without a development certificate,
	and it fails the *build*, not the run — "has entitlements that require
	signing with a development certificate" is what a missing certificate looks
	like, however unrelated it sounds.

	One gotcha worth knowing, because the error is silent: an Apple Development
	certificate is issued by WWDR G3, and if only the older (expired) WWDR
	intermediate is in the keychain the certificate is inert —
	`security find-identity -v -p codesigning` reports no valid identities and
	codesign says "unable to build chain to self-signed root". The fix is to
	install AppleWWDRCAG3.cer from apple.com/certificateauthority.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!-- The App Sandbox key is deliberately absent, not false: reading Outlook
	     over Apple events needs it off, and the sanctioned scripting-targets
	     route requires the target app to publish scripting access groups, which
	     Outlook does not. See DESIGN.md sections 1 and 8.6. -->
	<!-- Hardened Runtime (not the sandbox) is what gates sending Apple events.
	     Note that it is genuinely on now: ad-hoc builds used to disable it. -->
	<key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
	<true/>

	<!-- iCloud sync (DESIGN.md, CloudKit appendix). The container identifier
	     must match CloudSyncSettings.defaultContainerIdentifier; the entitlement
	     gate refuses to mirror if they ever drift apart. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-container-identifiers</key>
	<array>
		<string>iCloud.com.rihscb.Planner</string>
	</array>
	<key>com.apple.developer.icloud-services</key>
	<array>
		<string>CloudKit</string>
	</array>
	<!-- Push is what makes another Mac's change arrive without a relaunch.
	     Mirroring still works without it, just lazily. Change to "production"
	     for a Developer ID or App Store build. -->
	<key>com.apple.developer.aps-environment</key>
	<string>development</string>
</dict>
</plist>
